      "checks": {
        "base_3x3": "Both bases tiled 3x3, unrotated, at 1x and nearest-neighbour 4x. Entire native composites and four covering 4x panels per base inspected, including horizontal/vertical joins and intersections. No hard wrap seams, square boundary grid or distracting compositional repeat. Summer retains its quiet asphalt variation. Revised winter suppresses the previous two large signature slush islands: small irregular cool marks are distributed over subdued asphalt, without the previous paired 288px lobe cadence. A repeated texture is locatable on deliberate comparison, but no motif or grid commands attention at native size.",
        "built_up_layouts": "All three building groups in both seasons composited densely on their matching street base, then spaced apart. Six complete dense-to-sparse layouts inspected at 1x and in 36 covering 4x panels. Every source variant also inspected unobscured on native contact sheets and at 8x. Dense placement reads as a coherent contemporary settlement; sparse placement leaves the base exposed and reveals no distracting winter repeat. Overlap in the dense test and clipping at a review-panel boundary are test-layout effects, not source clipping.",
        "one_cell_8x2": "Six fixed-seed random 8x2 layouts inspected at 1x and 4x: city 0..5, slums 0..7, industry 0..5, summer and winter. Every eligible variant appears at least once in each layout. Continuous street underlay; no source-cell borders, seam rhythm or stamped ground grid. Multiple draws of the same sprite are intentional random placements, not near-duplicate source assets.",
        "every_file_8x": "All 76 complete sprite canvases inspected at exactly 8x in 38 labelled summer/winter pair pages. Both complete bases inspected through four covering 144x144-source quadrants at 8x; full-base 8x images also saved. Nearest-neighbour enlargement throughout.",
        "dimensions_placement_alpha": "All 78 expected files present, with required sizes. Both street bases are opaque 288x288. City 0..5: 48x48, 6..11: 48x96, 12..15: 96x96. Slums 0..7 and industry 0..5: 48x48; remaining sprites: 96x96. Sprite alpha is binary, all 76 feet end one row above the bottom, 75 bounding boxes are exactly centred and one is offset only 0.5px. No blank, cropped or floating source sprite.",
        "edges_blur_noise": "8x inspection finds crisp pixel steps, controlled outlines and no visible matte fringe, halo, stray edge pixels or antialiasing. Roof corrugation and metal ribs describe material rather than undirected noise. Small window/door/roof shapes remain readable at 1x. Bases use low-contrast pixel clusters; the winter texture is subdued enough to remain background rather than all-over camouflage.",
        "lighting_palette": "Compared modern reference markers 0..3 and modern-house, approved out/modern markers, round-2 city/slums/industry, paddies, and summer/winter grass and plains bases/details at 1x and 4x. Warm cream concrete, muted terracotta/brick, blue glass, cool metal, olive plants and dark outlines fit the approved palette. Upper/left surfaces carry highlights and right walls are darker. Winter snow is consistent cool blue-white; no new palette clash or reversed lighting found.",
        "diversity": "No exact decoded-image duplicates among the 78 targets. Native sheets and 8x pairs distinguish shopfronts, gabled house, balconies, framed glass offices, wedge building, skylit mall, parking deck, courtyard block and stepped office. Slums vary roof pitch, patching, tarps, stairs, height and compound arrangement. Industry varies warehouses, sawtooth roofs, tanks, silos and processing machinery. Similar material colours and repeated window conventions do not make these near-duplicate buildings.",
        "winter": "All 38 winter sprites retain their summer structure with snow placed on roofs, ledges, steps and equipment. None is blank or an inconsistent replacement. Winter pavement reads as cleared cold asphalt with restrained salt/slush traces; it is intentionally quieter than roof snow and remains legible underneath it. The formerly failed broad cloudy pair no longer dominates the 3x3 or sparse layouts. No need for every street pixel to become white to match the brief, which specifies snow on roofs and ledges.",
        "not_applicable": "The named Part 4 contains no peaks or tree sprites, so peak lattice/range and forest composites have no scoped input. It also contains no crater, classical-ruin, cyberpunk or autumn set. Egg-crate peaks, Swiss-cheese craters, classical ruins, stamped cyberpunk grids, flat orange autumn and identical tree crowns are therefore not applicable; no files from other parts were substituted or adjudicated."
      },
